mooth. Pointwise uniqueness follows from Lemma \\ref{lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec}.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[Existence and uniqueness of horizontal lifts] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a686f72697a6f6e74616c2d6c6966742d6f662d766563746f722d6669656c64\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ahorizontal-lift-tangent\">↗ def:horizontal-lift-tangent</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ahorizontal-space\">↗ def:horizontal-space</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asubmersion\">↗ def:submersion</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-metric\">↗ def:riemannian-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahorizontal-lift-linear-spec\">↗ lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahorizontal-lift-smooth-in-data\">↗ lem:horizontal-lift-smooth-in-data</a> <p></p>Every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$X\\in \\mathfrak X(M)$\">$X\\in \\mathfrak X(M)$</span> has a unique smooth horizontal lift <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde X$\">$\\tilde X$</span> satisfying <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d\\pi _x(\\tilde X_x)=X_{\\pi (x)}$\">$d\\pi _x(\\tilde X_x)=X_{\\pi (x)}$</span>.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ahorizontal-lift-tangent\">↗ def:horizontal-lift-tangent</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahorizontal-lift-linear-spec\">↗ lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahorizontal-lift-smooth-in-data\">↗ lem:horizontal-lift-smooth-in-data</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ahorizontal-space\">↗ def:horizontal-space</a> \\sketch Define <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde X_x=L_x(X_{\\pi (x)})$\">$\\tilde X_x=L_x(X_{\\pi (x)})$</span>. The right-inverse and orthogonality properties give the lift conditions. In local tangent trivializations, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$L_x$\">$L_x$</span> is the smooth lift of the smooth families representing <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde g_x$\">$\\tilde g_x$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d\\pi _x$\">$d\\pi _x$</span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde X$\">$\\tilde X$</span> is smooth. Pointwise uniqueness follows from Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahorizontal-lift-linear-spec\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a686f72697a6f6e74616c2d6c6966742d6c696e6561722d73706563\">7</a>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:tangent-space-horizontal-vertical-splitting","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:horizontal-lift-realizes-horizontal-vector","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:horizontal-lift-tangent","title":"def:horizontal-lift-tangent","label":"def:horizontal-lift-tangent"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:horizontal-space","title":"def:horizontal-space","label":"def:horizontal-space"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:submersion","title":"def:submersion","label":"def:submersion"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric","title":"def:riemannian-metric","label":"def:riemannian-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec","title":"lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec","label":"lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-lift-smooth-in-data","title":"lem:horizontal-lift-smooth-in-data","label":"lem:horizontal-lift-smooth-in-data"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:horizontal-lift-realizes-horizontal-vector","title":"prop:horizontal-lift-realizes-horizontal-vector","label":"prop:horizontal-lift-realizes-horizontal-vector"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prob:horizontal-vector-fields","title":"prob:horizontal-vector-fields","label":"prob:horizontal-vector-fields"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter7#prop:oneill-formula","title":"prop:oneill-formula","label":"prop:oneill-formula"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:horizontal-lift-of-vector-field","title":"prop:horizontal-lift-of-vector-field","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[Existence and uniqueness of horizontal lifts]\n\\label{prop:horizontal-lift-of-vector-field}\n\n\\uses{def:horizontal-lift-tangent, def:horizontal-space, def:submersion, def:riemannian-metric, lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec, lem:horizontal-lift-smooth-in-data}\n\n\n\n\nEvery $X\\in\\mathfrak X(M)$ has a unique smooth horizontal lift $\\tilde X$ satisfying $d\\pi_x(\\tilde X_x)=X_{\\pi(x)}$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:horizontal-lift-tangent,lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec,lem:horizontal-lift-smooth-in-data,def:horizontal-space}\n\\sketch Define $\\tilde X_x=L_x(X_{\\pi(x)})$. The right-inverse and orthogonality properties give the lift conditions. In local tangent trivializations, $L_x$ is the smooth lift of the smooth families representing $\\tilde g_x$ and $d\\pi_x$, so $\\tilde X$ is smooth. Pointwise uniqueness follows from Lemma \\ref{lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec}.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:horizontal-lift-tangent","title":"def:horizontal-lift-tangent","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:horizontal-space","title":"def:horizontal-space","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:submersion","title":"def:submersion","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric","title":"def:riemannian-metric","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec","title":"lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-lift-smooth-in-data","title":"lem:horizontal-lift-smooth-in-data","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}